From 428df1d46a3d1041ba8073c04e52b8081060aede Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Munawar Rahman <msrahmanadam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 05:37:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: V3D (Pi 5) support: cap workgroups at 256, gate
 pathological pipeline compiles

- Cap all hardcoded 512/1024-invocation workgroups to 256 (V3D
  maxComputeWorkGroupInvocations); keep host wg_denoms and the
  SET_ROWS elements-per-workgroup divisor in sync.
- GGML_VK_MMV_MAX_COLS=N: report MUL_MAT with more than N result
  columns unsupported so it falls back to CPU. v3dv register
  allocation never terminates compiling the multi-column
  mul_mat_vec pipelines (>9 min per pipeline); n=1 compiles and
  passes test-backend-ops.
- GGML_VK_DISABLE_FLASH_ATTN: v3dv aborts on subgroup reduce fmin
  in the FA shaders (unimplemented NIR intrinsic).
- GGML_VK_NODES_PER_SUBMIT: cap command buffer size (diagnostic).
- test-backend-ops: GGML_TEST_PRINT_ERR=1 prints the measured NMSE
  for every case, not just failures.

All 45 GPU-runnable ops of granite-4.0-1b Q4_0 (exported real graph
shapes) pass the NMSE gate vs the CPU backend on V3D 7.1.10.2.
Decode at -ngl 6 is temp-0 coherent; full offload is incoherent on
both v3dv and llvmpipe with stock bb28c1f as well (pre-existing
upstream defect, not V3D-specific).
